== (8) cycle census over Z for the shortcut map T (|x| <= 2 * 10^5) and the conjectural zeta function ==
 cycles (element of least modulus, T-period = halvings A, odd steps p): [(0, 1, 0), (-1, 1, 1), (1, 2, 1), (-5, 3, 2), (-17, 11, 7)]
 Artin-Mazur zeta of T on Z, conjecturally exact: zeta(z) = 1 / (1 - z^1) (1 - z^1) (1 - z^2) (1 - z^3) (1 - z^11)
 T-periods [1, 1, 2, 3, 11]: 1, 1, 2, 3 are F_1..F_4 and 11 = L_5 (golden numerology, explained by the shared prefix [1;1,1] of log_2 3 and phi and the Lucas mediant 11/7)
== (9) Cayley-Hamilton, associated Mersenne numbers, the resultant reading, spectra, Zsigmondy ==
 Q^4 = [[2, 3], [3, 5]], trace 7 = L_4, det 1; Q^8 - L_4 Q^4 + (-1)^4 I = 0: True  (the owner: phi^8 + 1 = 7 phi^4)
 Q^5 = [[3, 5], [5, 8]], trace 11 = L_5, det -1; Q^10 - L_5 Q^5 + (-1)^5 I = 0: True  (the owner: phi^10 - 1 = 11 phi^5)
 associated Mersenne numbers |O_j| = |L_j - 1 - (-1)^j| = |det(Q^j - I)|, j = 0..16 (OEIS A001350): [0, 1, 1, 4, 5, 11, 16, 29, 45, 76, 121, 199, 320, 521, 841, 1364, 2205]
 doubling chain j = 2^k: |O_j| = 5 F_(j/2)^2: [(4, 5, 5), (8, 45, 45), (16, 2205, 2205), (32, 4870845, 4870845)] ; traces L_(2^k) = 3, 7, 47, 2207 (the historian chain), L_(2n) = L_n^2 - 2 for even n
 resultants: Res(t^7 - 1, t - 2) = -127 = 2^7 - 1; Res(t^5 - 1, t^2 - t - 1) = -11 = |O_5| = L_5; Res(t^3 - 1, 4t - 3) = 37 = 2^6 - 3^3 (constant-valuation ray v = 2, p = 3)
